    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance to help responders locate the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with posts or reflective delineators on both sides to define the entry point, especially in low-light or smoky conditions.\n• Trim trees and shrubs along the driveway to maintain clearance for emergency vehicles along the full length of the drive.\n• Keep the driveway surface clear of parked vehicles, equipment, or debris so emergency vehicles can travel its full length without obstruction.\n• Identify and maintain a turnaround area near the main residence so fire and emergency vehicles can reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Post the address number visibly at or near the detached structure if it sits at a distance from the main residence, so responders can identify it as a separate building on the property.\n• Thin dense vegetation along the driveway edges so responders on foot can move alongside vehicles if needed.\n• Keep a clear path between the main residence and the detached structure so responders can move between the two buildings without pushing through overgrown areas.\n• If a gate controls driveway access, equip it with a Knox Box or responder-compatible lock so emergency crews are not delayed at the entrance."
